	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42284</id><title>Floods and Food Security: The Hidden Cost to Crops and Soil</title><updated>2026-02-06T12:56:14-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42284" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/floodsfoodsecurity.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/floodsfoodsecurity.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
URBANA, Illinois, US, February 6 (IPS)  - &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/south-africa-flood-rain-disaster-8b5744763b6a41ca479c0c9a8254b051&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://apnews.com/article/south-africa-flood-rain-disaster-8b5744763b6a41ca479c0c9a8254b051&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1770462906541000&amp;usg=AOvVaw09okLEDC8JFVlVIvKNSo0I&quot;&gt;South Africa&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cddgq9z4899o&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cddgq9z4899o&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1770462906541000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ZAkBis2zIrSMcskulapbm&quot;&gt;Mozambique&lt;/a&gt;, and Zimbabwe are currently experiencing severe flooding. According to the World Health Organization, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.afro.who.int/news/around-13-million-people-affected-severe-flooding-southern-africa&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.afro.who.int/news/around-13-million-people-affected-severe-flooding-southern-africa&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1770462906541000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2HjOV1AalQWjTrDYr7p3yF&quot;&gt; 1.3 million people have been affected&lt;/a&gt;. In addition, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-people-killed-or-missing-after-floods-in-southern-africa/g-75567349&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-people-killed-or-missing-after-floods-in-southern-africa/g-75567349&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1770462906541000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3J7y0pxdvw8qD8Sm5Bmesd&quot;&gt; hundreds of people have died &lt;/a&gt;, infrastructure has been destroyed, access to health services has been disrupted, and the risks of water- and mosquito-borne diseases are rising.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42284&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Floods and Food Security: The Hidden Cost to Crops and Soil”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/floodsfoodsecurity-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42283</id><title>WHO Launches $1 Billion Appeal Amid Funding Shortfalls and Widening Gaps in Healthcare Access</title><updated>2026-02-06T11:10:51-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42283" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/The-158th-session_.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/The-158th-session_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, February 6 (IPS)  - On February 3, the World Health Organization (WHO) launched its &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.who.int/emergencies/funding/health-emergency-appeals/2026&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;2026 global appeal&lt;/a&gt; to help millions of people living in protracted conflicts and humanitarian crises access lifesaving healthcare. Following a trend of sharply declining international funding, the agency warns that it is becoming increasingly difficult to respond to emerging health threats, including pandemics and drug-resistant infections.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42283&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “WHO Launches $1 Billion Appeal Amid Funding Shortfalls and Widening Gaps in Healthcare Access”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/The-158th-session_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42282</id><title>UN Human Rights Office Launches USD 400 million Appeal to Address Global Human Rights Needs</title><updated>2026-02-06T10:37:49-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42282" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/An-artist-in-Colombia_.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/An-artist-in-Colombia_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
GENEVA, February 6 (IPS)  - The UN High Commissioner for Human Rights Volker Türk has launched a USD 400 million funding appeal for 2026 to address global human rights needs, warning that with mounting crises, the world cannot afford a human rights system in crisis.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42282&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN Human Rights Office Launches USD 400 million Appeal to Address Global Human Rights Needs”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/An-artist-in-Colombia_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42281</id><title>UN Security Council: Reform or Irrelevance</title><updated>2026-02-06T10:12:29-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42281" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/Denis-Balibouse_.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/Denis-Balibouse_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
BRUSSELS, Belgium, February 6 (IPS)  - In early January, an emergency UN Security Council &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.securitycouncilreport.org/whatsinblue/2026/01/venezuela-emergency-meeting.php&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;meeting on Venezuela&lt;/a&gt; followed a familiar path of paralysis. Members clashed over the US government’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://lens.civicus.org/venezuela-democracy-no-closer/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;abduction of Nicolás Maduro&lt;/a&gt;, with many warning it set a dangerous precedent, but no resolution came.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42281&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN Security Council: Reform or Irrelevance”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/Denis-Balibouse_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42280</id><title>Is the US Planning to Throw a Lifeline to a Sinking UN?</title><updated>2026-02-06T09:35:14-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42280" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/Is-the-US-Planning_.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/Is-the-US-Planning_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, February 6 (IPS)  - The current UN financial crisis, described as the worst in the 80-year-old history of the world body, triggers the question: is the US using its financial clout defaulting in its arrears and its assessed contributions to precipitate the collapse of the UN?
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42280&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Is the US Planning to Throw a Lifeline to a Sinking UN?”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/Is-the-US-Planning_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42290</id><title>From shelter to strength: How disaster refuges protect lives in Palau</title><updated>2026-02-06T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42290" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/06-02-2026-IOM-Palau-01.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/06-02-2026-IOM-Palau-01.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The small Pacific Ocean island of Palau is helping communities build resilience against the dangers of climate change-driven extreme weather with the establishment of a network of emergency refuges – thanks to support from the United Nations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42290&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “From shelter to strength: How disaster refuges protect lives in Palau”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/06-02-2026-IOM-Palau-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42289</id><title>Pakistan: Guterres condemns deadly suicide bombing at Islamabad mosque</title><updated>2026-02-06T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42289" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/06-02-2026-UN_Photo-Pakistan-Islamabad.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/06-02-2026-UN_Photo-Pakistan-Islamabad.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The UN Secretary-General on Friday strongly condemned an attack on worshippers at a mosque in Pakistan’s capital, Islamabad, after an explosion during prayers reportedly killed dozens and injured many more.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42289&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Pakistan: Guterres condemns deadly suicide bombing at Islamabad mosque”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/06-02-2026-UN_Photo-Pakistan-Islamabad.jpeg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42288</id><title>Nuclear disarmament at breaking point as mistrust grows – but hope remains</title><updated>2026-02-06T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42288" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/27-8-2029_Kazakhstan%20Paintings.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/27-8-2029_Kazakhstan%20Paintings.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The global system governing nuclear disarmament is facing its most serious crisis in decades, driven by growing mistrust among major powers and the steady erosion of arms control agreements, a senior disarmament expert has warned.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42288&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Nuclear disarmament at breaking point as mistrust grows – but hope remains”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/27-8-2029_Kazakhstan%20Paintings.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42287</id><title>Ukraine war keeps nuclear safety on a knife-edge, UN watchdog warns</title><updated>2026-02-06T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42287" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/25-04-2024-IAEA-inspectors.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/25-04-2024-IAEA-inspectors.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Attacks on Ukraine’s power system highlight how the ongoing war threatens the safety of the country’s nuclear facilities, the head of the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) warned on Friday. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42287&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Ukraine war keeps nuclear safety on a knife-edge, UN watchdog warns”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/25-04-2024-IAEA-inspectors.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42286</id><title>Guterres welcomes resumption of Iran-US talks</title><updated>2026-02-06T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42286" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/13-01-2022_UNSPLASH_Iran.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/13-01-2022_UNSPLASH_Iran.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UN Secretary-General António Guterres on Friday welcomed the resumption of talks between Iran and the United States. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/06/42286&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Guterres welcomes resumption of Iran-US talks”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/13-01-2022_UNSPLASH_Iran.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry></feed><!-- 0.0015s -->